(LST-81: because nesting always copies, a list can never truly contain
 itself: `append x to x.` copies x's state at the moment of the append
 and appends that copy, so x ends up [[]] one level deep, not a cycle
 (LANGUAGE.md:2517-2519, 0.4.15, #111). Replaces withdrawn LST-33 (the
 0.4.14 and earlier text described this same program as building a real
 cycle, capped at print depth 64).
